WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.760
Which part of a plant is a carrot?

2
00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.320
And what does that part do?

3
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.240
A bag of groceries and one big drawing let your child find out.

4
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.760
Fruits and vegetables come from plant parts.

5
00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.080
Each part had a job.

6
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:23.160
Your child practices sorting, looking for clues, and changing a guess after checking

7
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.160
it.

8
00:00:24.433 --> 00:00:26.273
Check for food allergies first.

9
00:00:27.573 --> 00:00:30.053
Use pictures for foods your child needs to avoid.

10
00:00:31.493 --> 00:00:36.253
Gather paper, markers, a carrot, asparagus, lettuce, broccoli, an apple, and a

11
00:00:36.253 --> 00:00:42.613
tomato. Add canned beans or frozen peas, a firm potato without green skin or

12
00:00:42.613 --> 00:00:44.593
sprouts, and celery with leaves.

13
00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:48.647
Help your child draw the plant and label each part.

14
00:00:49.887 --> 00:00:55.327
Wash the produce. You cut the apple and the tomato across the middle, so the seeds

15
00:00:55.327 --> 00:00:58.347
show. Leave everything else whole.

16
00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.230
Hold up one food at a time.

17
00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:04.890
Ask, 'Which part of the plant do you think this is?'

18
00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:06.910
Let your child place it on the drawing.

19
00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.570
Don't correct anything yet.

20
00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:12.170
That first sort is the guess.

21
00:01:13.233 --> 00:01:14.993
Now go back and look for clues.

22
00:01:16.473 --> 00:01:19.973
A tomato grows from a flower and holds seeds, so it is a fruit.

23
00:01:21.333 --> 00:01:24.813
Look for thin side roots on the carrot or marks where they were trimmed.

24
00:01:26.193 --> 00:01:27.393
Ask, 'What is your clue?'

25
00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:30.027
Here is one for you.

26
00:01:31.107 --> 00:01:32.747
Look closely at a head of broccoli.

27
00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:35.627
Which part of the plant are you holding?

28
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.670
Each small green bump is a flower bud.

29
00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:48.170
Left to grow, the buds open into small yellow flowers.

30
00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:50.990
So broccoli moves to the flower.

31
00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:53.633
Now check the trick cards.

32
00:01:54.973 --> 00:01:56.833
Look at the potato's eyes with your child.

33
00:01:58.153 --> 00:02:00.373
Each eye is a bud, like a bud on a stem.

34
00:02:01.673 --> 00:02:03.653
A potato is an underground stem.

35
00:02:05.113 --> 00:02:06.853
Celery is mostly long leaf stalks.

36
00:02:08.093 --> 00:02:09.413
Look for the leaves at the top.

37
00:02:10.417 --> 00:02:12.897
Point to each part and ask what it does.

38
00:02:14.137 --> 00:02:15.137
Roots take in water.

39
00:02:16.477 --> 00:02:17.577
Stems hold the plant up.

40
00:02:18.917 --> 00:02:20.217
Leaves make food using light.

41
00:02:21.817 --> 00:02:23.897
Flowers make seeds, and the fruit holds them.

42
00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.520
Stay with your child the whole time food is out.

43
00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.920
You do all the cutting and put the knife away.

44
00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.360
Tasting is optional.

45
00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:38.200
Check allergies first, and cut small pieces onto a clean plate.

46
00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:40.980
Never taste raw potato.

47
00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.440
Wash your hands and have your child wash theirs when you finish.

48
00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:49.910
Keep small food pieces away from children under four.

49
00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:55.890
Whole peas, beans, and hard chunks of raw carrot or apple are choking hazards.

50
00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:59.290
Call nine one one if a child is choking.

51
00:03:00.433 --> 00:03:05.213
End by asking, 'Which part of the plant is a carrot, and what does that part do?'

52
00:03:05.893 --> 00:03:09.933
If your child is unsure, go back to the drawing and check the carrot together.

53
00:03:11.093 --> 00:03:14.193
The root holds the plant in the ground and takes in water.
